<title>SPAIN: Spain's BCH names new vice-chairman.</title>
<headline>Spain's BCH names new vice-chairman.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Central Hispanoamericano approved the chairman's proposal to name Angel Corcostegui Guraya as vice chairman.</p>
<p>Corcostegui replaces the retiring Luis Coronel de Palma, the bank said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Corcosetegui joined BCH as chief executive in July 1994, having left Banco Bilbao Vizcaya.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
